  "description": "The previous path had become worn slippery and unsafe after many years of use resulting in slips involving occupiers and visitors including an elderly family member. The dangerous path has been removed leaving the hardcore underneath. No parking area has been formed and no additional front garden area has changed. The replacement finish comprises of decorative black ice stone chippings chosen as a modest and sympathetic material, light grey and dark grey colours. Lawn remains to either side of the path as existing. The proposal is minor in scale, preserves the character of the frontage and maintains safe pedestrian access to the dwelling. Planning permission is respectfully requested.",
